{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbCJ5h2nRaWTHkxDYx5b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PzdRkjqz6YxKuf2LQq5jYQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_5\nSRC=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/models/terminal_discounted_streak_lapse.py\necho mirror_symmetry_terminal_streak_lapse > $D/model_name.txt\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of `terminal_discounted_streak_lapse` (statistically tied with the incumbent): each person still judges a sequence as more random the closer its alternation rate lies to their own ideal switching rate, still penalises lopsided heads/tails counts and the most striking streak (with the run still in progress at the end weighed by a shared factor) by weights of their own, and still guesses on some trials at a personal lapse rate. The one change is that people notice mirror symmetry: a sequence of four or more flips that reads the same backwards as forwards (a palindrome such as HTTTTTTH or HHHTTHHH) looks designed, and so less random, by a shared weight — addressing the critique that people choose the palindrome of a pair less often than the alternation, balance and streak terms predict.\nEOF\npython3 - \"$SRC\" \"$D/candidate.py\" << 'EOF'\nimport sys\ns=open(sys.argv[1]).read()\ns=s.replace('''\"\"\"Personal ideal alternation, balance weight, streak aversion and lapse, with the final run weighed apart.\n''','''\"\"\"Mirror-symmetry aversion added to terminal_discounted_streak_lapse.\n\nHypothesis: each person judges a sequence as more random the closer its\nalternation rate lies to their own ideal, penalises imbalance and the most\nstriking streak (final run weighed by a shared factor) by weights of their own,\nguesses at a personal lapse rate, and additionally